# The negation of a ball with a one-limb center: exact, the radius unchanged.
kernel:        ball_neg_1
input:         cx
input:         rx
output:        cz
output:        rz
value:         -cx
requires:      nonneg rx
ensures:       encloses cz rz -x x=cx,rx
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Ball.v ball_neg_1_correct
source:        midpoint-radius negation (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

cz = neg(cx)
rz = copy(rx)
